    "created_at": "2015-09-05T14:00:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-05T14:00:32Z",
    "body": "Thanks, that is good to know.\n\nAs far as the desired behavior goes, in Gecko we are planning to use the response tainting of the `Response` object passed to `respondWith` to override the mode flag in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#cors-enabled-fetch such that the `\"opaque\"` and `\"opaqueredirect\"` values are treated as if the `mode` flag is `\"No CORS\"`.  Would that make sense?\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
